# Workflow plan step D3 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): the DEME run flow. The Run page says it builds by itself when
# the source changed; the rebuild switch and "Run with an OpenFOAM case" are behind Advanced. The GPU as nvidia-smi gives it,
# and the run's size against the free memory from the project's last run (.qc-gpu: particles, MB it took).
action go.new
wait-until page New case
click new-prog:deme
wait 5
click label:Settle a bed
wait 5
click clone-name
key A ctrl
type d3bed
click clone-go
wait-until page Overview timeout 10
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
wait 60
assert text It builds by itself before running when the driver's source
assert not text Run with an OpenFOAM case
assert not text Rebuild anyway
assert text GPU: 
screenshot $OUT/d3_run.png
click pr-advanced
wait 10
assert text Rebuild anyway, from scratch
assert text Run with an OpenFOAM case
shell echo "20000 700" > .qc-gpu
wait 30
assert text The last run took 700 MB for up to 20000 particles
screenshot $OUT/d3_advanced.png
